  "result": "All 6 tests pass (4 existing plus the 2 new ones in tests/test_t2.py).\n\n**What changed** in `catalog/service.py`:\n\n- **`find(substring)`** returns copies of records whose title contains the substring, compared with casefold, in creation order.\n- **`export()`** returns a JSON array of the records in creation order, built from the existing list method.\n- **`import_(dump)`** parses the array, validates each record has exactly id, title, and author with a non-empty string id, then inserts them keeping their ids. It works on empty or populated catalogs.\n\n**Two design points worth knowing:**\n\n- **Id collisions raise ValueError** and leave the catalog untouched, since all validation happens before any insertion. Silently overwriting an existing record seemed the wrong default for a \"keep the ids\" import.\n- **The sequential counter is advanced past any imported decimal id.** Without this, importing ids \"1\" and \"2\" into a fresh catalog and then calling create would have produced a duplicate \"1\". Non-decimal ids from another id strategy are accepted as-is and do not affect the counter.",
